Default the minimum OS a darwin/amd64 link stamps to 10.9, not Go's 13.0. Every darwin/amd64
link goes through the external linker (patches 0011/0012), and the go.o Go hands it carried
LC_BUILD_VERSION minos 13.0; Apple's old ld64 said nothing, but lld (clang22) warns on every link
"go.o has version 13.0.0, which is newer than target minimum of 10.9.0". The final binary's floor
was already 10.9 (the CC wrapper's -mmacosx-version-min); this only makes the object agree.
-ldflags=-macos=X still overrides (flags are parsed after init). Other targets, the cross
toolchain's own darwin_arm64 tools included, keep Go's default.

--- src/cmd/link/internal/ld/macho.go.orig
+++ src/cmd/link/internal/ld/macho.go
@@ -450,6 +450,16 @@
 	macSDK = macVersionFlag{26, 2, 0}
 )
 
+// Mavericks: a darwin/amd64 link defaults to a 10.9 minimum OS, the floor every Mavergreen
+// darwin/amd64 binary carries. The external linker (lld) warns on every link when the go.o
+// Go hands it says 13.0 while the target minimum is 10.9. -macos still overrides: flags are
+// parsed after init. Other targets keep the default above.
+func init() {
+	if buildcfg.GOOS == "darwin" && buildcfg.GOARCH == "amd64" {
+		macOS = macVersionFlag{10, 9, 0}
+	}
+}
